  "reason": "The best result so far is config_036 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) at 0.715 accuracy. The strongest evidence from RNA-only experiments shows scvi_n200 + multiprofile + avgpool is the optimal RNA pipeline, and adding imagenet_vit_l with concat fusion yields the best overall result. The key untested design choice within this top configuration is the fusion strategy: config_037 is identical to config_036 except it uses weighted fusion instead of concat. This is a clean single-variable comparison that isolates whether learned weighting of modalities improves over simple concatenation. With only 2 experiments remaining, testing this directly exploits the strongest evidence while resolving an important uncertainty about fusion. If weighted fusion matches or beats concat, it informs the final experiment; if not, we confirm concat is optimal and can spend remaining budget on the next most impactful axis (e.g., transformer aggregation in config_038)."
}

